From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Tue, 16 Sep 2026 01:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: recore: clock the SPL's CPU to 648 MHz, not 816

Reflash #88 (USB reads wedging in u-boot) and Rebuild #85 (eMMC -110)
both follow from the frequency the SPL picks for the firmware phase.

sunxi_board_init() only clocks the CPU up "if we are reasonably assured
it's being powered with suitable core voltage" - it checks power_failed,
which the PMIC code sets. Recore builds with SUNXI_NO_PMIC, so nothing
ever sets the CPU rail and nothing can fail: power_failed stays 0 and the
SPL clocks to CONFIG_SYS_CLK_FREQ, 816 MHz by default on sun50i,
whatever the rail happens to be at. Measured on the bench board, the
AXP803 comes up with DCDC2/DCDC3 (paralleled, vdd-cpux) at 1.10-1.12 V -
exactly the A64 OPP minimum for 816 MHz, and on a warm reboot it is
whatever Linux last left there.

Measured on A8 s/n 0498, the board that reproduces #88 readily, counting
EHCI timeouts and uInitrd loads per boot from the serial capture:

  816 MHz (stock)      17 boots, 9 with EHCI timeouts, 2 of 3 USB boots
                       failed to load uInitrd, 1 dead in the SPL on -110
  816 MHz @ 1.20 V     fails the same way, so this is not rail margin:
                       the SPL was patched to set DCDC2/3 to 1.20 V and
                       the very next USB boot lost uInitrd
  648 MHz              20/20 USB boots clean, 0 timeouts, uInitrd in
                       2178-2180 ms every time
  408 MHz              31 boots clean, 0 timeouts

This only affects the firmware phase. Linux reprograms PLL1 from its own
OPP table with the matching voltage, so the board still runs at full
speed; it costs about 0.3 s in the SPL and u-boot.

648 MHz is a documented A64 OPP point (1.04 V), so it is in spec even at
the power-on rail voltage, which 816 MHz is not.
---
 configs/recore_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/recore_defconfig b/configs/recore_defconfig
--- a/configs/recore_defconfig
+++ b/configs/recore_defconfig
@@ -33,3 +33,4 @@ CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y
 CONFIG_PREBOOT="mw.l 0x01f01400 0x00020102; usb reset; run bootcmd_usb0"
 CONFIG_CMD_BMP=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="run distro_bootcmd; setenv stdout serial,vidconsole; echo; echo 'BOOT FAILED: nothing to boot from'; echo 'The eMMC did not answer. Connect the serial header for detail.'"
+CONFIG_SYS_CLK_FREQ=648000000
